  "body": "This brand-new single-level home offers a bright, modern feel with a layout that makes everyday living simple. With three well positioned bedrooms, great indoor-outdoor flow, and a sunny deck for relaxing or entertaining, it's a smart choice for families, first-home buyers, or anyone seeking a comfortable home in the growing Strathmill community.\r\n\r\nKey features include:\r\n*  10 Year Master Build Guarantee\r\n*  Three bedrooms, including a master with ensuite and walk-in wardrobe\r\n*  Master bedroom with ranch slider opening directly to the deck\r\n*  Upmarket open plan kitchen, dining and lounge with great natural light\r\n*  Large deck offering easy outdoor living and entertaining\r\n*  Single internal-access garage plus one off-street park\r\n*  Low maintenance 197sqm section, ideal for busy households\r\n\r\nThe open-plan living area forms the heart of the home, with ranch sliders creating a seamless connection to the generous deck -  perfect for weekend barbecues or unwinding in the afternoon sun. All three bedrooms are thoughtfully positioned for privacy. The remaining bedrooms are serviced by a modern family bathroom, and the easy-care section keeps maintenance to a minimum.\r\n\r\nSet within the fast-growing Strathmill neighbourhood, this home offers convenient access to motorway links for easy travel north or south. Orewa Beach, local cafes, schools, shops and restaurants are all just a short drive away, giving you the best of relaxed coastal living with everyday convenience.\r\n\r\nHow to find Awa Uru Road:\r\n* From the motorway, travelling North: Take exit 394 from SH 1, continue on Grand Drive and take first road to your left onto Flavell Drive, continue into the Strathmill Development and turn right, at the top take first left and continue to see the road to your right being Awa Uru Road:  https://maps.app.goo.gl/oSrN4H1EQNZ2LarR6\r\n\r\n* From Orewa: Follow West Hoe Heights until you see the Strathmill sign. Turn left onto Awa Uru Road and follow the signs.\r\n\r\nFor more information or to book a private viewing, contact Shaun Burnett on 021 871 252 or Ann Park on 021 151 8458",
